          "role": "Ärztin",
          "avatar": "👩‍⚕️"
        }
      },
      "lines": [
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Ich arbeite heute im Frühdienst. Arbeitest du auch hier?",
          "en": "I am on the early shift today. Are you working here too?"
        },
        {
          "who": "A",
          "de": "Ja. Ich kontrolliere den Verband. Die Patientin wartet im Zimmer.",
          "en": "Yes. I check the dressing. The patient is waiting in the room."
        },
        {
          "who": "N",
          "de": "Wir dokumentieren die Werte. Herr Yilmaz atmet ruhig.",
          "en": "We document the readings. Mr Yilmaz is breathing calmly."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "Endings in the present",
      "story": [
        "Take the stem and add an ending. <b>ich -e, du -st, er/sie/es -t, wir -en, ihr -t, sie/Sie -en</b>.",
        "If the stem ends in <b>-t</b> or <b>-d</b>, put an <b>e</b> before -st and -t, so you can hear the ending: du <b>arbeitest</b>, er <b>arbeitet</b>.",
        "If the stem ends in <b>-s, -ss, -ß</b> or <b>-z</b>, du only adds <b>-t</b>: du <b>heißt</b>."
      ],
      "tables": [
